@f12o/dsh-dots README · @f12o/dsh-dots：- a private workspace and sandbox root;
- a home session that survives restarts;
- an operating contract loaded through the normal `AGENTS.md` mechanism;
- bounded `MEMORY.md` injection on every assignment;
- durable schedules that wake a cold session;
- an execution-time tool allowlist;
- a host attribution so one controller can manage dots on several DSH machines;
- a root-level sidebar panel with creation, status, assignment, memory, schedule, and archive actions.

@f12o/dsh-dots README · Dots panel：The bundle ships a browser panel as well as Host tools. Installing it adds a
root-level **Dots** entry to the sidebar beside Workspaces and Automation tasks,
and a main panel that:

@f12o/dsh-dots README · Dots panel：- shows every local and remote dot with host reachability and live status;
- creates a dot on a local or remote host, including its model and reasoning
  effort;
- opens a local dot's Session, or a remote host's own DSH UI;
- queues assignments, appends durable memory, creates an every-N-seconds
  schedule, and archives a dot;
- follows the DSH locale: English and Japanese copy are bundled, with the
  shipped language selector switching both live.

@f12o/dsh-dots README · Creation：If Workspace registration fails, the dot still runs from its directory. If Session creation fails
after a Workspace was created, the partial directory is kept and the error names it; retry with a
new dot or clean up manually.

@f12o/dsh-dots README · Assignment：`dot_assign` resolves the dot, resumes a cold session through the Session controller, reads the tail
of `MEMORY.md` (up to `maxMemoryBytes`), and queues a `[DOT ASSIGNMENT]` message through
`agent.followup()`. The source kind is `dot`. A running dot receives the assignment on a later turn;
one dot processes assignments serially. The controller records `lastAssignedAt` and
`assignmentCount`.
